---
import ToolsLayout from '../../layouts/ToolsLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { toolsIndexUrl, editorialPolicyUrl } from '../../lib/tools';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd, type BreadcrumbItem } from '../../lib/articles';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';

const canonical = new URL(editorialPolicyUrl('en'), SITE.url).href;
const idHref = new URL(editorialPolicyUrl('id'), SITE.url).href;

const breadcrumb = [
  { label: 'Tools', href: toolsIndexUrl('en') },
  { label: 'Editorial Policy' },
] satisfies BreadcrumbItem[];

const sections = [
  { id: 'method', label: 'Research-based method' },
  { id: 'scoring', label: 'Hybrid scoring' },
  { id: 'independence', label: 'Editorial independence' },
  { id: 'trademarks', label: 'Trademarks & logos' },
  { id: 'accuracy', label: 'Accuracy & corrections' },
];
---

<ToolsLayout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="How XDIRGA TOOLS reviews digital tools: research-based method, hybrid scoring rubric, editorial independence, and trademark notes."
  lang="en"
  canonical={canonical}
  hreflang={{ en: canonical, id: idHref }}
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbJsonLd(breadcrumb)]}
>
  <div slot="sidebar">
    <nav
      class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5"
      aria-label="On this page"
    >
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-text">On this page</p>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm">
        {
          sections.map((s) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`#${s.id}`} class="text-text-secondary transition hover:text-primary">
                {s.label}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <a
        href={toolsIndexUrl('en')}
        class="mt-5 block rounded-xl bg-primary px-4 py-2.5 text-center text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-primary-hover"
      >
        Browse all tools
      </a>
    </nav>
  </div>


  <Breadcrumb items={breadcrumb} />

  <header class="mt-6">
    <h1 class="font-display text-[2.3rem] leading-[1.1] font-semibold text-text sm:text-[2.9rem]">
      Editorial Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[1.02rem] leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
      XDIRGA TOOLS is a curated directory of digital tools with honest, research-based reviews.
      This page explains exactly how we work — what we check, how we score, and what we never
      do.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section id="method" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-text">Research-based method</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-text">
      Every review is based on research of public, official sources: the vendor's own
      documentation, pricing page, terms of service, and privacy policy, plus reputable
      independent coverage where available. Each tool page lists its sources and the date the
      information was last verified.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-text">
      We do <strong>not</strong> claim hands-on testing. We never label a tool "Tested" and we
      never describe using a product ourselves unless that is genuinely the case. Scores reflect
      what the documentation and public record show, not personal trial experience.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="scoring" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-text">Hybrid scoring</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-text">
      Each tool receives an editorial score from 0 to 10, built from a 100-point rubric across
      six dimensions. The total rubric points divided by 10 give the headline score, so the
      breakdown and the score always agree.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-5 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[480px] border-collapse text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-border text-left">
            <th class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Dimension</th>
            <th class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-semibold text-text">Max points</th>
            <th class="py-2.5 font-semibold text-text">What it measures</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium text-text">Usefulness</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-text-secondary">25</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 text-text-secondary">How well the tool solves a real problem for its intended audience.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium text-text">Features</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-text-secondary">20</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 text-text-secondary">Breadth and depth of features, based on official documentation.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium text-text">Ease of use</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-text-secondary">15</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 text-text-secondary">How easy the tool is to learn and use day to day.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium text-text">Pricing &amp; value</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-text-secondary">20</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 text-text-secondary">What the free plan covers and whether paid plans are fairly priced.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium text-text">Platform &amp; accessibility</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-text-secondary">10</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 text-text-secondary">Availability across web, desktop, and mobile, plus accessibility.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium text-text">Transparency &amp; trust</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 text-text-secondary">10</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 text-text-secondary">Clear pricing, terms, privacy policy, and vendor track record.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-text">
      A dimension scored 0 is shown as "insufficient evidence" — meaning we could not find
      enough public evidence to assess it, not that the tool is bad at it. Scores are editorial
      assessments, not user ratings and not vendor claims.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="independence" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-text">Editorial independence</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-text">
      Reviews are written independently. Vendors do not pay for reviews, placement, or higher
      scores, and we do not accept sponsored content in the directory.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-text">
      Monetization is postponed entirely: there are no affiliate links, no sponsored listings,
      and no paid placements in XDIRGA TOOLS. If that ever changes, this page will say so
      before any monetized link appears.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="trademarks" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-text">Trademarks &amp; logos</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-text">
      Product names, trademarks, and logos shown in the directory belong to their respective
      vendors. Logos are used only to identify the product being reviewed (nominative use).
      Listing a tool does not imply endorsement by, or affiliation with, its vendor.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="accuracy" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-text">Accuracy &amp; corrections</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-text">
      Tool information reflects what was publicly available on the "last verified" date shown
      on each tool page. Features and prices change — when you find something outdated or
      wrong, tell us via the{' '}
      <a href="/kontak/" class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline">contact page</a>
      {' '}and we will re-check the official sources and correct the page.
    </p>
  </section>
</ToolsLayout>
